**Why this is safe**: `route_agent()` clones the base agent with a SUBSET of tools, but the FunctionTool objects are **shared references** (same `id()`). The wrapper's `on_invoke_tool` closure captures `self` (the AgentRuntime instance), not the agent. So looking up from `assistant_agent.tools` finds the SAME wrapper object regardless of routing.

